# TypeScript / Bun conventions (path-scoped)

Applied only when TS/TSX files are in context (progressive disclosure — keeps
the orchestrator prompt lean until relevant).

- Pure logic goes in a `*.ts` module with **no `@oh-my-pi/*` import** so it is
  unit-testable without the runtime (mirror `lib/peer-policy.ts` and the
  `buildHonchoTools` pure factory). The omp-coupled wrapper imports the pure core.
- Skill `bin/*.ts` are standalone Bun scripts: guard `if (import.meta.main)`
  around `process.exit(main(...))` so they can also be imported by tests.
- Respect `tsconfig` strictness: `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`,
  `verbatimModuleSyntax` (use `import type` for types), no implicit any.
- File writes that must be private use mode `0o600` and atomic temp-rename
  (see `specsafe.ts::atomicWrite`).
- Prefer `node:`-prefixed builtins. Prefer `spawnSync`/`spawn` over shelling
  out string-concatenated commands.
- Every new behavior lands test-first (see TDD Iron Law). Tests live under the
  nearest `test/` dir and run via `bun test`.
